## 34. Posterior Mean of the Diffused Gaussian Mixture

The target result of Problem 2(d) has three equivalent forms.

### Form 1 — Score-Based Denoising

$$
\boxed{
\mathbb E[x_0\mid x_t]
=
\frac{
x_t+(1-\bar\alpha_t)s_t(x_t)
}{
\sqrt{\bar\alpha_t}
}
}
$$

### Form 2 — Mixture Score Representation

$$
\boxed{
\mathbb E[x_0\mid x_t]
=
\frac1{\sqrt{\bar\alpha_t}}
\left[
x_t-
(1-\bar\alpha_t)
\sum_k
w_{k,t}(x_t)C_{k,t}^{-1}x_t
\right]
}
$$

### Form 3 — Weighted Linear Denoisers

$$
\boxed{
\mathbb E[x_0\mid x_t]
=
\sum_k
w_{k,t}(x_t)
\sqrt{\bar\alpha_t}
\Sigma_kC_{k,t}^{-1}x_t
}
$$

Define each component denoiser as

$$
G_{k,t}
=
\sqrt{\bar\alpha_t}
\Sigma_kC_{k,t}^{-1}
$$

Then

$$
\boxed{
\mathbb E[x_0\mid x_t]
=
\sum_k w_{k,t}(x_t)G_{k,t}x_t
}
$$

Relevant identities for the homework derivation:

$$
\sum_k w_{k,t}(x_t)=1
$$

$$
C_{k,t}
=
\bar\alpha_t\Sigma_k+
(1-\bar\alpha_t)I
$$

$$
I-bB^{-1}=aAB^{-1}
$$

The detailed equivalence proof is reserved for Round 2.

