## 39. Score-Based Sampling

### Gradient Ascent

$$
x_{n+1}=x_n+\eta s(x_n)
$$

Repeated gradient ascent tends toward stationary points
rather than sampling the full probability distribution.

### Langevin Dynamics

$$
\boxed{
x_{n+1}
=
x_n+\eta s(x_n)
+\sqrt{2\eta}\epsilon_n
}
$$

where

$$
\epsilon_n\sim\mathcal N(0,I)
$$

| Term | Function |
|---|---|
| $\eta s(x_n)$ | Guide samples toward locally higher density |
| $\sqrt{2\eta}\epsilon_n$ | Introduce randomness and exploration |

Under suitable conditions, continuous Langevin dynamics
has the target distribution as its stationary distribution.

The discretized algorithm provides an approximation.

Langevin dynamics and DDPM sampling are related but
are not identical algorithms.

