## 42. Important Conceptual Distinctions

### Single-Step vs. Cumulative Diffusion

| Single-Step | Cumulative |
|---|---|
| $\alpha_t$ | $\bar\alpha_t$ |
| From $x_{t-1}$ to $x_t$ | From $x_0$ to $x_t$ |
| Noise variance $1-\alpha_t$ | Noise variance $1-\bar\alpha_t$ |

### Prior vs. Posterior Mixture Weights

| Prior | Posterior |
|---|---|
| $\pi_k$ | $w_{k,t}(x_t)$ |
| Fixed | Observation-dependent |
| Used in forward marginal | Used in reverse transition, score and posterior mean |

### Conditional vs. Marginal Score

| Conditional Score | Marginal Score |
|---|---|
| $\nabla_{x_t}\log q(x_t\mid x_0)$ | $\nabla_{x_t}\log q(x_t)$ |
| Depends on clean sample | Depends on noisy sample and time |
| Individual noise target | Conditional expectation of noise target |

### MMSE vs. MAP vs. Sampling

| MMSE | MAP | Sampling |
|---|---|---|
| Posterior mean | Posterior mode | Random posterior sample |
| Minimizes squared error | Maximizes density | Preserves distribution |
| May average multiple modes | Selects a mode | Represents uncertainty |

### Gaussian Component vs. Gaussian Mixture

| Property | Single Gaussian | Gaussian Mixture |
|---|---|---|
| Score | Affine; linear if zero mean | Generally nonlinear |
| Denoiser | Affine; linear if zero mean | Generally nonlinear |
| Conditional covariance | Observation-independent | May depend on observation |
| Exact reverse transition | Gaussian | Gaussian mixture |

